  "articleBody": "Comparing residential painting estimates involves much more than reviewing the bottom-line price. Quality interior painting depends heavily on what happens before a single paint can opens.\n\nGuide to Evaluating Painting Estimates\n- Overview: A thorough contractor builds surface preparation directly into their scope, ensuring your paint adheres properly and lasts for years.\n- Key Benefits: Comprehensive prep work eliminates visible wall patches, seals hairline cracks, and creates crisp lines along baseboards, doors, and ceilings.\n- Process Breakdown: Proper work starts with surface inspection, patching drywall holes, sanding smooth, cleaning dust, and masking trim and floors. Primer is applied where bare drywall or stains show, followed by controlled coats of paint and careful cleanup.\n- Real Examples: An estimate that skips patching nail pops or drywall imperfections might look cheaper upfront, but flaws show under lighting once fresh paint dries.\n\nWhat to Prepare Before You Start\nList every room needing work, note drywall flaws, and mention high-wear spots like hallways. To review an interior painting plan, contact HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
